<https://loze-ontology.org/isOriginIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Origin In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A top-level ontology largely inspired - with a few deviations and additions - by the four-category ontology outlined by the philosopher E. J. Lowe (2006), supplemented with the concept of a schematic particular explored by Eddy Zemach (1970)" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHeldIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Entity> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Parthood> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The core participants in a parthood are the part (loze:isComponentIn) and the composite (loze:isCompositeIn)" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasContent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/ConcreteParticular> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Differently from Schematic particulars, a concrete particular only occupies one place or location at a time: my copy of War and Peace occupies one slot in my bookcase right now; I can only occupy one place at a time; a unit of Toyota Corolla is in one place at a time; a particular performance of Beethoven's Symphony No 9 takes place in one and only one venue" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAffectedIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAffectedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Affected In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHeldIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isThemeIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAgentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHeldIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isTopicIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Joe is the topic in an identity check, an electrical system is the topic of an electrical safety report, cancer (as a schematic particular or a class of eventualities) is the topic in a cancer research, liberty is the topic of John Stuart Mill's essay 'On Liberty', a book (in abstraction from its copies) is the topic of a review" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstrumentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasCause> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasProduct> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e and a particular p if and only if p is a product in e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasHost> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e and a particular p if and only if p is the host in e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/PlaceOccupation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDestinationIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The change in question does not need to be a movement, but it can be a qualitative or quantitative change too: for example, if an eventuality consists in one object becoming more similar to another one, the latter will be the destination" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAgentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The killer is the agent in a killing, the mechanic is the agent in the repair of the car, Joe is the agent in Joe's walking, the baker is the agent in the making of the bread" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Constitution> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/Composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDeterminationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Determination Of" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasConcretization> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a schematic particular s and a concrete particular c if and only if c is a concretization of s" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Constitution> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Constitution" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isTopicIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an entity e and an eventuality e' if and only if e is a subject matter of cognition or meaning in the context of e' " .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Constitution> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "In formal mereology, one particular being 'entirely made up' by repeated occurrences, means that it is identical to the mereological sum of those occurrences: as an approximation, this means that its only parts are those occurrences and the parts of those occurrences; more rigorous definitions can be found in the philosophical literature on formal mereology" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHeldIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Held In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasComposite> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasCause> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isWaypointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHolderIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Holder In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Containment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An eventuality in which a particular is positioned within and physically constrained by another object" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isTopicIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasParticipant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Entity> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAgentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a thing t and an eventuality e if and only if t acts or causes changes in some thing in the context of e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasAgent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Thing> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasSetting> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Constitution> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Object" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasStage> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHolderIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Entity> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/Entity> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isReferencePointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a particular p and a composition c if and only if p composes some other particular in the context of c" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasConcretization> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Concretization" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasContent> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isContentIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/SchematicParticular> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Composition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Composition" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDeterminationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/SchematicParticular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isThemeIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDestinationIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasDestination> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e and a particular p if and only if p is the destination in e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Containment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasProduct> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Aggregate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Objects are also typically material, but aggregates differ from objects because they are not unified by an internal organisation, function or form" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A particular entity that is a way of being or a modification of one or more other entities - qualifying them or making them be or go in a certain way - and is individuated by those entities" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Place> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "There is an obvious sense in which even objects can host other particulars: for example, a house can host people and artefacts; likewise, a tank can host amounts of liquid; however, places host things by being occupied by them, whereas objects host things by having them within themselves - that is, by having them occupying the place that they enclose" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/SchematicParticular> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "An schematic particular has the force of a determinant with regard to its concretizations: the structure of Beethoven's Symphony No 9 dictates the structure of its performances; the specifications of the Toyota Corolla are the benchmark for the features of its units; the chemical properties of water determine the behaviour of concrete portions of water" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A red apple participates in its redness; Socrates participates in his wisdom; two spouses participate in their marriage; a killer, the victim, and the gun all participate in a killing; Italy, Austria and Germany all participates in Austria being located between Italy and Germany" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/PlaceOccupation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The core participants in a place occupation are the place (:isHostIn) and the particular entity that occupies it (:isHostedIn)" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Eventuality" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "An eventuality is not general, but is linked to its participants - that is, the entities that bear it or are involved in it; the wisdom of Socrates is numerically distinct from the wisdom of Diogenes, and they existed at different times; the redness of this apple is distinct from the redness of that other apple, and so on" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStageOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "In other upper-level ontologies, relations like this are considered special cases of parthood, since the stages of an eventuality can be viewed as its 'temporal slices'; however, we prefer to suspend the judgment about whether the stages of an eventuality are to be considered among its parts" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/PeriodOfTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Two period of time can have exactly the same duration and yet be distinct period of time, because they have distinct beginnings and ends; for example, this hour and the next hour are two distinct periods, despite having the exact same duration of 60 minutes" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasOrigin> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
_:n76b48cac102f40e997a1be148c172908b12 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://loze-ontology.org/Constitution> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isComponentIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAgentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
_:n76b48cac102f40e997a1be148c172908b4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/PeriodOfTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A thing that is individuated by its coordinates across the temporal axis" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCauseOf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHostIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isWaypointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isOriginIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Aggregate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Aggregate" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasRecipient> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasCause> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e and an eventuality e' if and only if e' is a cause of e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSettingIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDeterminationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/SchematicParticular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isProductIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Every eventuality that has a product also has some agent" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Entity> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "It corresponds to owl:Thing" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasDetermination> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCauseOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Multiple eventualities can entertain the relation :isCauseOf with a given eventuality, since an eventuality can have more than one cause" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isConcretizationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/SchematicParticular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasAffected> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Thing> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Composition> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#unionOf> _:n76b48cac102f40e997a1be148c172908b11 .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isReferencePointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "In ordinary talk, the reference point of a movement is often not mentioned because it's identified by default with the Earth - or some Earth-based reference framework" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHostIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isReferencePointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The scope of this thematic relation is not limited to motion, but also encompasses other types of changes as well as comparisons: for example, if an eventuality consists in an object being larger than another one, the larger object will be the theme and the other will be the reference point" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasProduct> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Product" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCompositeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a particular p and a composition c if and only if p has as component some other particular in the context of c" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasHeld> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isOriginIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/SchematicParticular> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Differently from classes, schematic particulars share their main features with their instances; for example, a book has chapters just like its copies, a piece of music has the same harmonic structure as its performances, an alphabetic character has the same shape as its inscriptions, a car model has similar features as its units" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Entity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isBeneficiaryIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStageOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Given an eventuality e and a period of time t, e can have at the most one stage that occurs from the start to the end of t" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAffectedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The victim is affected in a killing, the cake is affected in an eating, the car is affected in the repair, the house is affected in an alteration" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isBeneficiaryIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Beneficiary In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Object> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "An object persists over time as long as it preserves the internal organisation, function, or form that individuates it; as long as that is preserved, the parts of the objects and their types can change without causing the object to go out of existence" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Aggregate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/Thing> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasHolder> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Holder" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasComposite> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasProduct> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isProductIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAffectedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "A given thing can be both agent and affected in the same eventuality: for example, a person washing themselves is both agent and the affected thing in a washing; in a handshake greeting, both persons are both agents (since they are shaking the other person's hand) and affected (since their own hand is being shaken)" .
_:n76b48cac102f40e997a1be148c172908b11 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://loze-ontology.org/Parthood> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSettingIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasDetermination> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/SchematicParticular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Parthood> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "An arm being part of a person, a wall being part of a house, a compressor being part of a refrigerator, a wood board being part of a table, a nucleus being part of an atom, Mars being part of the solar system, the lithosphere being part of the Earth, a movement being part of symphony, hydrogen atom being part of water molecule" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasComposite> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isCompositeIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstrumentIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasCause> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCompositeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "In my arm being part of my body, my arm is the component and my arm is the composite; in a heap of sand having an individual grain as part, the heap is the composite and the grain is the component; in the composition of water by hydrogen, water is the composite and hydrogen is the component" .
_:n76b48cac102f40e997a1be148c172908b10 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isConcretizationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The concretizations of War and Peace are its copies, the concretizations of Beethoven's Symphony No 9 are its performances, the concretizations of Sachertorte are the individual Sachertorte, the concretizations of a software are its installed copies, the concretizations of the Toyota Corolla (as a car model) are its manufactured units" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasHeld> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e' and an entity e if and only if e is held in e'" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAgentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "A given thing can be both agent and patient in the same eventuality: for example, a person washing themselves is both agent and patient in a washing; in a handshake greeting, both persons are both agents (since they are shaking the other person's hand) and patient (since their own hand is being shaken)" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Thing> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCompositeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasReferencePoint> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isReferencePointIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Composition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipientIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a particular p and an eventuality e if and only if some other particular is transferred or put under the hold of p in the context of e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasDestination> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasRecipient> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e and a particular p if and only if p is a recipient in e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an entity e and an eventuality e' if and only if e' determines, modifies or qualifies e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAgentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "An agent doesn't need to be a person, a living being or some other object that we would intuitively consider 'animated' " .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSettingIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The organisation is the setting of a presidency, a living being is the setting in which an organ is vital, a wall is a partition in a house" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isWaypointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "An intermediate stop in a travel, the ducts linking the supply point to a distribution point" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHolderIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "the person or organisation is the holder in a possession or ownership; the manager is the holder in a management relationship with the managed employee" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Parthood> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Parthood" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isWaypointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Component" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/PlaceOccupation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "In a place occupation, the host is always a place, rather the object enclosing it - say, the interior of a refrigerator, rather than the refrigerator itself" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isProductIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasOrigin> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e and a particular p if and only if p is the origin in e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasDestination> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Destination" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
