<https://loze-ontology.org/isContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Content In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The liquid is the content in its containment by a tank, the fluid is the content when flowing in a duct" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasAgent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isTopicIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/PeriodOfTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Period Of Time" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isBeneficiaryIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCauseOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An entity that is not a class or type of entities" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasHost> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Host" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHolderIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/SchematicParticular> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Similarly to classes, schematic particulars are not bounded to one particular location at a time: as a rule, a schematic particular is wholly present wherever one of its concretizations is present; War and Peace is present wherever one of its copies is present; water is present wherever one or more H2O molecules are present; the Toyota Corolla is present wherever one of its units is present" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasHost> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isHostIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStageOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The construction of the foundations of a house is a stage of the construction of the whole house, the preparation of the dough is a stage in the making of a pizza, the positioning of the explosive is a stage in the demolition of a building, the fermentation of the must is a stage in the production of wine" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstrumentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Instrument In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDeterminationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a schematic particular x and another schematic particular y if and only if x has all the essential properties of y together with further essential properties that y lacks" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasAgent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDeterminationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The Toyota Corolla Hatchback is a determination of the Toyota Corolla; the 1869 version of War and Peace is a determination of War and Peace; Apocalypse Now Redux is a determination of Apocalypse Now; heavy water is a determination of water; anthracite is a determination of coal; carbon-14 is a determination of carbon" .
_:n76b48cac102f40e997a1be148c172908b7 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://loze-ontology.org/Object> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isReferencePointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The possibility of absolute motion is controversial in theoretical physics and philosophy; however, this matter is operationally irrelevant, because in practice motion can only be assessed relative to a reference framework" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasInstrument> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isThemeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Theme In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isThemeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "In a marriage, both spouses are themes; in the case of a glass lying on a table, the glass is the theme; in the case of an amount of liquid contained in a tank, the amount of liquid is the theme; in the case of somebody owning a real estate, the real estate is theme" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Place> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/Thing> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCompositeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Composite In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Place> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The matter that is hosted in a place makes no difference for the individuation of that place: a room remains in existence irrespective of whether it hosts an absolute vacuum, a few pieces of furniture and regular air, or a giant load of cotton wool" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isProductIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
_:n76b48cac102f40e997a1be148c172908b2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHolderIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an entity e and an eventuality e' if and only if e controls or is super-ordinated to some other entity in the context of e' " .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasTopic> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isTopicIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Entity> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAffectedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipientIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Recipient In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Containment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A box containing eggs, a glass containing a portion of water, a dwelling containing pieces of furniture" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipientIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipientIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The payee is the recipient in a payment, the buyer is the recipient in a property conveyance, the addressee is the recipient in a shipping, the donee is the recipient in a donation" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Containment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
