<https://loze-ontology.org/hasProduct> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHostIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The house is the host in a residency or occupation, the tank is the host in the containment of a liquid, the duct is the host in the flow of a fluid, the place is the host in a position or location" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Intuitively, the participants in an eventuality can be viewed as the entities that are involved in it or play some role in it" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Aggregate> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasTheme> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e and a particular p if and only if p is a theme in e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAgentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Thing> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasContent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e and a particular p if and only if p is the content in e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isOriginIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a particular entity p and an eventuality e if and only if p is the initial point of a movement or change in the context of e" .
