<https://loze-ontology.org/Constitution> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An eventuality that consists in one particular being entirely made up by repeated occurrences of a given schematic particular" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasTopic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasWaypoint> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isWaypointIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isBeneficiaryIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The beneficiary is often going to be the recipient too, but there are exceptions; consider a case in which a household is awarded a grant for the energy upgrade of their house, and the grant is paid to an energy upgrade company: in that scenario, the company is the recipient of the grant, but the household is the beneficiary" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Particular" .
