<https://loze-ontology.org/hasStage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasInstrument> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Instrument" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHostIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Host In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasWaypoint> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e and a particular p if and only if p is a waypoint in e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isReferencePointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "In the case of John being taller than Dan, Dan is the reference point; in the case of an object falling down from the top of a tower, the top of the tower is the reference point; in the case of a vehicle moving on the surface of Earth, Earth - or some Earth-based geolocation framework - is the reference point" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasHeld> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Held" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Aggregate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A chunk of wood, a waterbody, the liquid contained in a tank, a heap of sand, the global petrol supply" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Aggregate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A thing that is individuated by some stable material composition or spatial contiguity" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The redness of this apple, the wisdom of Socrates, the marriage between Napoleon and Josephine, the stabbing of Caesar from Brutus, my walk from my house to a grocery shop, the Earth being positioned between Venus and Mars, an engine being fuelled with an amount of gasoline" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isConcretizationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Concretization enables schematic particulars to be located vicariously, by being located where their concretizations are; in general, a schematic particular is wholly present wherever one of its concretizations is present; since it can have multiple concretizations at the same time, a schematic particular can be located in multiple places at the same time" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Object> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A human, a horse, a molecule, a table, a computer, a planet, a paracetamol tablet" .
