<https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Entity> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasStage> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e and an eventuality e' if and only if e' is a stage of e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isProductIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "A product does not need to be a concrete particular, but it can also be a schematic particular: for example, a document or a book (in abstraction from its copies) is the product of a writing endeavour" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isBeneficiaryIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "People with cancer are the beneficiaries in a donation to cancer research, a household is the beneficiaty in an allocation of subsidies for energy upgrades work to a company" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStageOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Stage Of" .
