<https://loze-ontology.org/isOriginIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasDestination> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasDetermination> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/SchematicParticular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isConcretizationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/ConcreteParticular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasComponent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipientIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasConcretization> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "In my arm being part of my body, my arm is the component and my body is the composite; in a heap of sand having an individual grain as part, the heap is the composite and the grain is the component; in the composition of water by hydrogen, water is the composite and hydrogen is the component" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAffectedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Every eventuality that has an affected thing also has some agent" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasWaypoint> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
_:n76b48cac102f40e997a1be148c172908b9 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:n76b48cac102f40e997a1be148c172908b10 .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isWaypointIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasDetermination> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isDeterminationOf> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isTopicIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Since a cognition can be about abstractions, the topic of an eventuality can also be a class or a schematic particular" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "This is intended as a broad, comprehensive category that encompasses the entities that in other ontologies and category systems are variously called 'qualities', 'attributes', 'relations, 'events', 'processes', 'facts', 'specifically dependent continuants' etc..." .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Containment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "In a containment, the core participants are the container (loze:isHostIn) and the content (loze:isContentIn)" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasHost> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/SchematicParticular> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A particular that is not bounded to one spatial location at a time and that can be concretized by concrete particulars" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStageOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between two eventualities e and e' if and only if e is a stage or phase in the occurrence of e' " .
<https://loze-ontology.org/PeriodOfTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/Thing> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Component In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasWaypoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isBeneficiaryIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isProductIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The house is the product in a construction work, the cake is the product in the context of baking, molecules are the products in a chemical synthesis, the zygote is the product in the fertilization of a female gamete from a male gamete" .
_:n76b48cac102f40e997a1be148c172908b8 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:n76b48cac102f40e997a1be148c172908b9 .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasHost> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isReferencePointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a particular p and an eventuality e if and only if p is the term of reference point or the reference framework for a movement, change, or comparison in the context of e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasRecipient> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDestinationIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSettingIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "This thematic relation is intended for those eventualities that consist in roles, positions, or functions within a setting or an organised system; the participant that occupies the role is a theme in the eventuality" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasParticipant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Participant" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasTopic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Topic" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasInstrument> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e and a particular p if and only if p is an instrument in e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasRecipient> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Recipient" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Constitution> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "In a constitution, the core participants are the composite (loze:isCompositeIn) and the schematic particular that is repeated in it (loze:isComponentIn)" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isThemeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a particular p and an eventuality e if and only if p is in a certain state or occupies a position in the context of e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasBeneficiary> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/PlaceOccupation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A carrot occupying the interior of a refrigerator, a sofa occupying a living room, an amount of liquid occupying the interior of a tank" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasContent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Content" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isOriginIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The origin does not need to be a place, but it can be a thing or a period of time too" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isProductIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasWaypoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Waypoint" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstrumentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The instrument in an eventuality can also be a person: for example, the messenger is the instrument in the sending of a message" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasContent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasConcretization> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isConcretizationOf> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstrumentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The gun is the instrument in a killing, the hammer is the instrument in the driving of a nail, the vehicle is the instrument in a journey, a debit or credit card is the instrument in a payment" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSettingIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an object o and an eventuality e if and only if o is the setting or context in which e is the case" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Thing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isThemeIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasBeneficiary> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasStage> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isStageOf> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointUnionOf> _:n76b48cac102f40e997a1be148c172908b3 .
<https://loze-ontology.org/PlaceOccupation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An eventuality that consists in one particular entity occupying a place partly or entirely" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Thing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A particular entity that is not a way of being or a modification of other entities" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Parthood> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An eventuality that consists in one particular being part of another particular" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Place> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Place" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasDetermination> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a schematic particular x and a schematic particular y if and only if y is a determination of x" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasTheme> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isThemeIn> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isTopicIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Topic In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/Aggregate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "An aggregate can also be scattered across space - such as the total water reserve of England or the amount of methane used for heating my house over the last year - in which case its individuation is based on a combination of material composition and practical interests" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasTheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Theme" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasBeneficiary> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e and a particular p if and only if p is a beneficiary in e" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasComposite> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDestinationIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Destination In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/PeriodOfTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The year 1943, the 6th of May of 2005, any second or minute, the period that goes from the 3rd of May of 1467 to the 22nd of July of 1615" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isReferencePointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Reference Point In" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasHolder> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasSetting> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Setting" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/ConcreteParticular> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The distinction between concrete particulars and schematic particulars cuts across all the other divisions of the class :Particular: there are concrete objects and schematic objects, concrete eventualities and schematic eventualities, concrete aggregates and schematic aggregates, and so on" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isConcretizationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The concretizations of a schematic particular can deviate from it in various respects: for example, most performances of Beethoven's Symphony No 9 typically lasts between 65 and 75 minutes, but the 2018 performance from the Philarmonia Orchestra conducted by Benjamin Zander only lasts 58 minutes; in some cases, the deviation is merely an anomaly, but in other cases it entails that the concretization is defective, faulty, or bad, like a poorly made Sachertorte, or a faulty Toyota Corolla unit" .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCauseOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Cause Of" .
_:n76b48cac102f40e997a1be148c172908b4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCauseOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "A simple, informal test for assessing whether an eventuality e is cause of another eventuality e' is to ask whether e'occurs (also) because of e, or whether the occurrence of e' is explained (among the other things) by the occurrence of e; if the answer is affirmative, then e entertains loze:isCauseOf with e' " .
<https://loze-ontology.org/PeriodOfTime> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasHolder> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> .
